\fs36 Package.json : 
\f1\fs24 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
is a file located in the root directory of a Node.js project that contains essential information about the project. This file includes project dependencies, scripts, project details, and other important configuration information. The package.json file makes it easier to manage Node.js projects and install their dependencies. Useful for angular or react projects. The some parts are \
\
Name : project name\
Version : project version (1.0.0)\
Description\
Main : project path that will be started initially.\
Scripts : codes related with project\
Dependencies : for project needed\
devDependencies : for preprod needed\
Author : project owners\
License\
Repository	: GitHub , gitlab url\
Keywords : needed keywords for the project\
	\
\

\f0\fs36 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 Bash commands 2 (npm commands)\
